WEBVTT

00:01.814 --> 00:04.956
♪ it seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.024 --> 00:08.299
♪ is violence in movies
and sex on tv ♪

00:08.367 --> 00:11.543
♪ but where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.611 --> 00:14.552
♪ on which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.620 --> 00:18.397
♪ lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.465 --> 00:21.373
♪ lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.440 --> 00:22.944
♪ all the things that make us ♪

00:23.012 --> 00:24.215
♪ laugh and cry ♪

00:24.283 --> 00:27.457
♪ he's... A...
Fam... Ily... Guy! ♪

00:43.138 --> 00:44.542
Oh, uh, it sure was nice of you

00:44.610 --> 00:46.582
To invite us out on your yacht,
mr. Pewterschmidt.

00:46.650 --> 00:48.019
It's not a boat,
it's a yacht.

00:48.088 --> 00:50.393
Oh, I'm sorry, I thought
you said it was a boat.

00:53.337 --> 00:55.108
Wow, it's beautiful
down there.

00:55.176 --> 00:57.649
I just can't believe it
really looks like this.

00:57.717 --> 00:59.655
Stewie: Boy, the fish tank
at day care

00:59.723 --> 01:02.163
Really nailed it.

01:02.230 --> 01:04.670
Lois, are you feeling
all right?

01:04.739 --> 01:07.680
I'm just a little seasick,
that's all.

01:07.748 --> 01:09.351
(vomiting)

01:09.419 --> 01:11.191
Stewie:
Oh, my god!

01:11.258 --> 01:13.197
(laughing):
Oh, brian's eatin' it.

01:13.264 --> 01:14.868
Boy, that's a lot
of puke, lois.

01:14.936 --> 01:17.042
I ain't seen that much puke
since my bachelor party.

01:17.109 --> 01:18.245
Your what?

01:18.313 --> 01:19.917
My bachelor party.
What's that?

01:19.985 --> 01:21.789
You don't know what a
bachelor party is?
No!

01:21.856 --> 01:23.293
When you got married,
didn't you have,

01:23.362 --> 01:25.300
Like, a bachelor party
with all your friends?
My what?

01:25.368 --> 01:27.908
Oh, my god, well, we
are gonna fix that.

01:27.976 --> 01:29.412
Carter, I am gonna
throw you

01:29.480 --> 01:31.218
The best bachelor
party ever!

01:31.286 --> 01:33.157
Why would you do that?
'cause I'm your pal

01:33.225 --> 01:35.197
And I want to help.
Like cheeseburger helper.

01:35.265 --> 01:36.868
Hey there, peter.

01:36.936 --> 01:39.342
How would you like to take a
half a pound of hamburger

01:39.410 --> 01:42.184
And make a delicious meal
for the whole family?

01:42.252 --> 01:44.190
Sure!
Okay, then let's...

01:44.258 --> 01:46.196
Hold on there,
peter!

01:46.264 --> 01:48.202
I've got something
even better!

01:48.270 --> 01:50.208
Oh, really?
You bet.

01:50.277 --> 01:52.884
How would you like to take
a half pound of hamburger

01:52.951 --> 01:55.123
And make a delicious meal
for the whole family...

01:55.192 --> 01:57.130
With cheese?

01:57.198 --> 01:58.802
What?

01:58.869 --> 02:00.239
Wha... I-I don't...

02:00.307 --> 02:01.409
I-I could just take cheese

02:01.477 --> 02:02.980
And put it on the
thing he's doing.

02:03.049 --> 02:05.088
No! It won't be
the same!

02:05.155 --> 02:06.358
Look, he's my
brother.

02:06.425 --> 02:08.364
He didn't get enough
oxygen at birth.

02:08.432 --> 02:10.537
He's never gonna be quite in
step with the rest of us

02:10.605 --> 02:12.777
And this is sort of my way
of taking care of him.

02:12.846 --> 02:15.051
Well, that's nice of you,
but it was so much simpler

02:15.119 --> 02:16.890
When it was just you
and me doing our thing.

02:16.958 --> 02:18.763
I know, but just let
him have this one.

02:18.830 --> 02:21.270
Odds are he won't even come
back with the actual food.

02:21.338 --> 02:23.944
Okay, cheeseburger helper,
you're on.

02:24.012 --> 02:25.182
Yay!

02:25.250 --> 02:26.653
Cheese, cheese,
cheese!

02:26.721 --> 02:27.991
Yay!

02:28.058 --> 02:29.997
I'm so sorry for your burden.

02:30.064 --> 02:31.768
You're a good brother.

02:35.180 --> 02:37.185
(dance beat throbbing)

02:39.660 --> 02:41.799
So what do you think, carter?
You having a good time?

02:41.867 --> 02:43.872
I'm not sure what I'm supposed
to do with myself.

02:43.940 --> 02:45.210
I'm very uncomfortable.

02:45.277 --> 02:47.549
Why don't you get a lap dance,
mr. Pewterschmidt?

02:47.618 --> 02:50.058
No, peter's crippled friend,
I think I'm just gonna leave.

02:50.125 --> 02:51.394
This was a stupid idea.

02:51.462 --> 02:53.468
Aw, come on, you just gotta
relax and cut loose.

02:53.536 --> 02:55.206
Like those foreign
guys over there.

02:55.274 --> 02:57.714
I can't believe
I'm back at the horse.

02:57.781 --> 02:59.386
I had many drinks last night

02:59.454 --> 03:01.392
And I was so hung out
this morning.

03:01.460 --> 03:03.231
Aw, me, too,
friend.

03:03.299 --> 03:05.604
I was blowing chinks
like crazy.

03:05.672 --> 03:07.210
Boy, this is
fun, huh?

03:07.278 --> 03:09.116
Except for the fact we gotta
sit next to that woman

03:09.183 --> 03:10.519
Who came with her
co-workers.

03:10.588 --> 03:12.191
Huh, aren't we all pals?

03:12.259 --> 03:13.428
I work at the office.

03:13.496 --> 03:14.699
This is empowering.

03:14.767 --> 03:16.304
Maybe I'll get a dance, huh?

03:16.371 --> 03:18.376
You guys are probably gonna be
talking about this forever.

03:18.445 --> 03:20.249
A woman who's so cool
with all of this?

03:20.317 --> 03:21.486
Jackpot!

03:21.554 --> 03:23.058
All right, there's a
cute-looking one.

03:23.125 --> 03:24.295
Excuse me, miss?

03:24.363 --> 03:26.368
This older gentleman would
like a lap dance.

03:28.342 --> 03:30.112
What am I supposed to do?

03:30.181 --> 03:32.118
Nothing. You just sit there
and enjoy yourself.

03:32.187 --> 03:35.128
Do I, do I stick the money
directly inside of her?

03:35.196 --> 03:36.198
No, you do not.

03:36.265 --> 03:38.004
Why, have you done
that before?
(laughs)

03:38.071 --> 03:40.010
Doesn't go over.
When do I hit her?

03:40.077 --> 03:42.851
Oh, for crying out loud,
just drink this.

03:42.919 --> 03:45.861
And you, give this old bastard
the ride of his life.

03:45.928 --> 03:47.365
♪ ♪

03:47.433 --> 03:48.535
(laughing):
Yeah!

03:48.603 --> 03:49.672
All right, go, carter!
All right!

03:49.739 --> 03:51.176
Get some! Get some!

03:51.245 --> 03:53.450
Hey, joe, that's like
right in my (bleep) ear.

03:53.518 --> 03:55.055
Stop it! Peter, I-I...

03:55.122 --> 03:56.392
Whoa!

03:56.460 --> 03:58.231
Boy, she's bendy!

03:58.299 --> 04:00.137
(chuckles)
wow! Y-yes!

04:00.205 --> 04:01.975
Oh! Awesome!

04:02.044 --> 04:03.815
All right! Oh!

04:03.882 --> 04:05.821
(groaning)

04:05.888 --> 04:07.526
Oh, my god!
What's happening to him?

04:07.594 --> 04:09.867
I'm having a heart
attack-ack-ack-ack-ack-ack!

04:09.935 --> 04:11.940
You ought to know by now!

04:14.448 --> 04:15.885
Oh, my god!

04:15.953 --> 04:18.359
Is my father gonna be
okay, dr. House?

04:18.427 --> 04:20.265
He's in a coma, mrs. Griffin.

04:20.333 --> 04:21.936
And listening to the
sound of your voice,

04:22.004 --> 04:23.942
I'd say he's the lucky one.

04:24.010 --> 04:27.186
Oh, dear, I do hope there's
something to be done.

04:27.254 --> 04:29.192
Dr. House, if you're gonna
save this patient,

04:29.260 --> 04:30.463
You'll need this.

04:31.801 --> 04:34.775
Get this thing outta my sight!

04:35.780 --> 04:36.714
But wait a second!

04:36.783 --> 04:38.554
How are you gonna
play by the rules

04:38.621 --> 04:40.393
If you don't have
the rule boo-- oh...!

04:40.460 --> 04:43.402
My methods are a little
unorthodox, mr. Griffin.

04:43.469 --> 04:44.739
I think I can help.

04:44.807 --> 04:46.745
What are you doing?
My job.

04:46.813 --> 04:48.585
Sometimes people fake
being in a coma.

04:48.652 --> 04:49.921
This man's not.

04:49.990 --> 04:51.927
Unless of course, the first
punch knocked him out.

04:51.996 --> 04:54.469
In which case, we won't know
for some time.

04:54.537 --> 04:56.475
<i>House.
Road house.</i>

04:56.543 --> 04:58.280
That, too.

05:01.023 --> 05:02.794
Any word on carter's
condition yet?

05:02.862 --> 05:04.466
No, it's been three days

05:04.533 --> 05:06.305
And I'm really starting
to get worried.

05:06.373 --> 05:08.378
What if he's in a coma
for, like, 20 years

05:08.445 --> 05:11.053
And he comes out of the coma
and you guys are all dead,

05:11.121 --> 05:13.727
But I'm still alive and
I'm a famous race car driver,

05:13.795 --> 05:16.736
And he's like "aw, man,
stewie turned out awesome."

05:16.804 --> 05:18.409
And he comes to one
of my races

05:18.476 --> 05:20.748
And I'm so surprised
to see him there, I crash,

05:20.816 --> 05:22.754
And then I'm in a coma
for 20 years,

05:22.823 --> 05:25.263
And I wake up and
he's a race car driver.

05:25.331 --> 05:27.436
Stewie, do you want to
be a race car driver
when you grow up?

05:27.503 --> 05:29.375
Well, gosh, if you think
I'd be good at it.

05:29.443 --> 05:31.348
(doorbell rings)

05:32.385 --> 05:33.621
Hello, mrs. Griffin,

05:33.689 --> 05:35.527
I'm kenneth gould,
mr. Pewterschmidt's attorney.

05:35.595 --> 05:37.600
I'd like to talk to you
about a few things.

05:37.668 --> 05:39.773
As part of mr. Pewterschmidt's
estate planning,

05:39.841 --> 05:41.445
He has left video wills

05:41.513 --> 05:43.752
Applicable to a wide
variety of situations.

05:46.060 --> 05:47.497
Hello, if you're watching this,

05:47.564 --> 05:49.837
It means they didn't cut
the rope when I climaxed.

05:49.905 --> 05:51.208
As a result, I'm now dead.

05:51.276 --> 05:52.412
That's not it.

05:52.479 --> 05:53.849
If you're watching this one,

05:53.917 --> 05:55.655
It means the train wasn't
able to push the delorean

05:55.723 --> 05:58.664
Up to 88 miles per hour and
I'm still stuck in 1885.

05:58.732 --> 06:00.135
This could
take a while.

06:00.203 --> 06:02.141
Eaten by sharks
while snorkeling...

06:02.209 --> 06:04.347
...Stabbed to death
in a toys r us bathroom.

06:04.416 --> 06:06.555
...1940s roller skate
left in the hall.

06:06.622 --> 06:07.892
Death by chocolate.
(laughs)

06:07.960 --> 06:09.196
No, no, leave it in.

06:09.263 --> 06:10.868
Had a heart attack and have
slipped into a coma.

06:10.936 --> 06:12.138
Here we go.

06:12.206 --> 06:14.077
In that case,
I leave control of my company,

06:14.145 --> 06:16.451
Pewterschmidt industries,
to my daughter lois.

06:16.519 --> 06:17.655
What?!

06:17.723 --> 06:19.059
I don't know the first thing

06:19.128 --> 06:20.731
About running
a billion-dollar company.

06:20.799 --> 06:22.436
The board of directors
is fully prepared

06:22.504 --> 06:24.108
To run the company in
carter's absence,

06:24.176 --> 06:25.846
If that's what you'd
prefer, mrs. Griffin.

06:25.914 --> 06:27.886
Well, yes,
I think that'd be best.

06:27.954 --> 06:29.123
Well, now wait
a second, lois.

06:29.191 --> 06:31.129
I could run
the company.
You?

06:31.197 --> 06:33.135
You can't run a business
that size.

06:33.203 --> 06:34.974
You have no
experience.

06:35.042 --> 06:36.211
You know what
that is, lois?

06:36.280 --> 06:37.716
That's you playing
by the rule book.

06:37.784 --> 06:39.354
And I don't play
by the rule book.

06:39.422 --> 06:41.160
Right, dr. House?
Well, don't ask me.

06:41.228 --> 06:43.166
My superiors
think I'm crazy.

06:43.234 --> 06:45.172
(gibbering)

06:45.240 --> 06:46.843
Scared ya, didn't I?

06:46.911 --> 06:48.849
<i>House.
House.</i>

06:48.917 --> 06:50.522
And I'm gonna run
the company.

06:53.986 --> 06:55.756
Well, lois, I'm off
to my first day

06:55.825 --> 06:57.094
As a corporate bigwig.

06:57.162 --> 06:59.100
I'm not so sure about
this, peter.

06:59.168 --> 07:00.772
I mean, that's
daddy's company.

07:00.840 --> 07:03.246
He spent his whole life building
it from the ground up.

07:03.314 --> 07:05.586
And you don't know
anything about running
a big business.

07:05.655 --> 07:07.760
Whoa, whoa, thanks
for the vote of confidence.

07:07.828 --> 07:10.602
Geez, you're a bigger downer
than a german bedtime story.

07:10.670 --> 07:13.711
(male narrator reading
in german accent):

07:25.849 --> 07:27.152
And in addition,

07:27.220 --> 07:29.158
Pewterschmidt industries'
pharmaceutical division

07:29.226 --> 07:30.663
Is up over 30%,

07:30.731 --> 07:32.836
Profits in new media have
doubled each quarter

07:32.904 --> 07:36.346
Over the past year, and our
stock is at an all-time high.

07:36.414 --> 07:37.717
All right, stand aside.

07:37.785 --> 07:38.922
I'll take it from here.

07:38.989 --> 07:40.125
Good afternoon, gentlemen,

07:40.192 --> 07:41.496
My name is peter griffin.

07:41.564 --> 07:44.973
I will be running the company
from hence here forth.

07:45.041 --> 07:47.146
Now, I want you all to lay
some business talk on me.

07:47.213 --> 07:48.450
I need ideas.

07:48.518 --> 07:50.724
What can we do to make this
quarter more quarterly?

07:52.463 --> 07:53.465
Well, come on, come on.

07:53.533 --> 07:56.374
(murmuring)
(coughs)

07:56.442 --> 07:58.548
Okay, I can see I'm gonna have
to get things rollin'.

07:58.616 --> 08:00.821
All right, we're gonna do an
exercise called the idea ball.

08:00.888 --> 08:02.693
I'm gonna toss a ball
to one of you,

08:02.761 --> 08:04.699
And whoever catches it, throw
out the first idea you got,

08:04.767 --> 08:06.405
Then pass the ball
to the next guy,

08:06.473 --> 08:08.678
And he throws out an idea
and so on. Everybody clear?

08:08.746 --> 08:10.785
Yeah.
(murmuring)

08:10.853 --> 08:12.556
All right, here we go.

08:13.895 --> 08:15.097
All right, abrams, whaddaya got?

08:15.166 --> 08:16.803
Abrams:
My lung's collapsing.

08:16.871 --> 08:19.679
You know what I'm hearin',
gentlemen?

08:19.746 --> 08:22.186
(sighs)
what's the best way to put this?

08:22.254 --> 08:25.262
What I'm hearing...

08:29.208 --> 08:31.481
What I'm hearin' is a
lot of yesterday talk.

08:31.549 --> 08:33.788
This isn't the way we're gonna
do things under my leadership.

08:33.856 --> 08:35.794
We are gonna turn
this company around.

08:35.862 --> 08:37.432
But, sir, the company's
doing fine.

08:37.500 --> 08:38.435
Better than ever, in fact.

08:38.503 --> 08:39.873
Mr. Pewterschmidt would...

08:39.941 --> 08:41.712
I don't care what mr.
Pewterschmidt would have done.

08:41.780 --> 08:42.749
We need to take risks.

08:42.816 --> 08:44.521
We need a complete overhaul.

08:44.589 --> 08:46.560
Gentlemen, you're all fired.

08:46.628 --> 08:47.965
(all gasp)
what?!

08:48.032 --> 08:49.736
There, now that I've got
your attention...

08:49.804 --> 08:51.007
You're all fired.

08:55.087 --> 08:57.293
Peter, what the hell
is going on?

08:57.361 --> 08:59.633
You fired everybody
at daddy's company?!

08:59.701 --> 09:01.372
You bet.
Are you outta
your mind?!

09:01.439 --> 09:03.043
Keep it up, lois,
I might fire you.

09:03.111 --> 09:04.381
You wouldn't.

09:04.448 --> 09:07.356
Does the name lacey chabert
mean anything to you?

09:07.424 --> 09:08.861
Okay, I'll behave.

09:08.929 --> 09:10.098
Yes, you will.

09:10.166 --> 09:11.603
Look, peter,
all I'm saying is,

09:11.671 --> 09:13.609
Those guys have been
with daddy for years.

09:13.677 --> 09:16.183
How are you supposed to run
that company without them?

09:16.251 --> 09:17.521
That's it, lois,
you're fired.

09:17.589 --> 09:19.125
Chris, you are
now meg's mother.

09:19.193 --> 09:22.971
Ooh, peter, your muscles
are so muscley.

09:23.038 --> 09:26.248
I am gonna plow you
so gross later.

09:29.291 --> 09:32.232
You are a team of executives
I can trust.

09:32.300 --> 09:34.238
Brian, quagmire, mort,

09:34.306 --> 09:35.910
You are gonna be
my creative team.

09:35.978 --> 09:38.385
You are gonna help me lead
this company into the future.

09:38.452 --> 09:40.290
Peter, we don't know
anything more than you do

09:40.358 --> 09:41.293
About running
a company.

09:41.361 --> 09:42.363
Hey, where's joe?

09:42.431 --> 09:44.269
I think he's still
outside.

09:45.640 --> 09:47.846
Hey, joe!
What're you doin' down there?!

09:47.914 --> 09:48.916
There's no ramp!

09:48.984 --> 09:50.421
I can't get inside!

09:50.488 --> 09:51.758
Well, we don't need him anyway.

09:51.826 --> 09:54.266
This company's gonna
make it on my ideas.

09:54.334 --> 09:56.105
Here are the products
we'll be unveiling

09:56.173 --> 09:57.408
In the new fiscal year.

09:57.477 --> 09:59.449
The african american
heart monitor.

09:59.516 --> 10:03.561
Heart monitor:
Yeah. Yeah. Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

10:03.628 --> 10:05.600
Aw, he dead.

10:05.668 --> 10:07.606
Jeremy irons cereal.

10:07.674 --> 10:11.117
If you're looking for
marshmallows, there are none.

10:11.185 --> 10:14.160
It's quite bland, I assure you.

10:14.228 --> 10:15.931
And scream in a box.

10:15.999 --> 10:17.937
(man screaming)

10:18.005 --> 10:19.543
I needed that today.

10:19.611 --> 10:21.783
And now,
new lady scream in a box.

10:21.850 --> 10:23.622
(woman screaming)

10:23.689 --> 10:26.431
Finally, a scream
that's right for me.

10:29.474 --> 10:31.479
Well, it's good to see
everyone's adapting

10:31.547 --> 10:33.518
To their new business roles.

10:33.586 --> 10:35.591
Brian, I like
your successories.

10:38.601 --> 10:40.139
I will.

10:40.207 --> 10:42.245
I will go get it.

10:44.887 --> 10:46.190
(knocking)

10:46.258 --> 10:48.196
Mr. Quagmire, the davidson
account is waiting for you

10:48.264 --> 10:49.366
In the conference room.

10:49.435 --> 10:50.537
All right, thanks, marlene.

10:50.605 --> 10:51.875
Tell 'em I'll be right in.

10:51.942 --> 10:55.285
All right, glenn,
time to go make millions.

10:56.389 --> 10:58.194
What happened
to you, man?

10:58.262 --> 10:59.832
I grew up!
That's what happened!

10:59.900 --> 11:01.503
What happened to the
free-loving quagmire

11:01.571 --> 11:03.677
Who was banging ten
chicks at a time?

11:03.745 --> 11:05.348
I still do that.

11:05.416 --> 11:06.953
Oh. Good.
Yup.

11:07.022 --> 11:08.124
Can I have
some money?

11:08.192 --> 11:09.762
Oh, get out
of here, you bum.

11:09.829 --> 11:10.999
Ah, all right.

11:13.841 --> 11:18.622
Heart monitor:
Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.
Yeah. Yeah.

11:18.690 --> 11:19.859
He's a'ight.

11:19.927 --> 11:21.497
Daddy, you're awake!

11:21.565 --> 11:23.671
Oh, carter,
I'm so relieved.

11:23.739 --> 11:24.908
(groans)
what happened?

11:24.976 --> 11:26.078
Where am I?

11:26.146 --> 11:27.917
Oh, you had
a heart attack, daddy,

11:27.985 --> 11:29.421
But you're
all right now.

11:29.489 --> 11:30.692
Heart monitor:
Yeah, he cool.

11:30.760 --> 11:31.895
What the hell
is that?!

11:31.963 --> 11:33.668
Oh, it's an african american
heart monitor

11:33.736 --> 11:34.838
Made by your company.

11:34.905 --> 11:36.242
What?!

11:36.310 --> 11:39.118
Yes, it has two settings:
Barry white and bill cosby.

11:39.185 --> 11:42.328
Bill cosby heart monitor:
Beep. Beep. Boop. Beep.

11:42.396 --> 11:44.133
My company makes
no such thing.

11:44.200 --> 11:46.741
Well, you see, daddy,
when you were in a coma,

11:46.809 --> 11:49.684
Peter stepped in and took charge
of pewterschmidt industries.

11:49.751 --> 11:52.291
Bill cosby heart monitor:
Zibida, zoobida, gebada,
bopada, zipity, ziggita,

11:52.359 --> 11:54.765
<i>Zagata, boopada, bopada,
ghost dad!</i>

11:57.374 --> 11:58.376
(sighs happily)

11:58.445 --> 11:59.847
Well, you made it, peter.

11:59.916 --> 12:01.218
You're a big shot.

12:01.286 --> 12:03.291
In charge of a whole bunch
of people.

12:03.360 --> 12:05.665
Peggy, hold my calls
for a few minutes, please.

12:05.733 --> 12:07.002
Peggy:
Yes, mr. Griffin.

12:07.070 --> 12:09.945
Well, buddy,
you're in love with peggy.

12:10.012 --> 12:11.449
What a mess.

12:11.517 --> 12:13.823
Griffin! Get the hell
out of my building!

12:13.891 --> 12:15.963
Holy crap, mr. Pewterschmidt,
you're okay!

12:16.030 --> 12:17.467
You're damn
right I'm okay,

12:17.536 --> 12:19.841
And I'm here to reassume
charge of my company.

12:19.909 --> 12:21.413
Maybe I don't want to leave.

12:21.481 --> 12:23.152
Maybe I like being a fat cat.

12:23.219 --> 12:24.456
What are you saying?

12:24.524 --> 12:25.960
I'm saying it's my company now,

12:26.028 --> 12:28.735
And it's better than it ever was
when you were running it.

12:28.804 --> 12:30.842
Security, we have a situation
in the conference room.

12:30.910 --> 12:33.015
I'll give you a
situation, you fat turd.

12:33.082 --> 12:35.222
Gentlemen, please remove
this man from the building.

12:35.290 --> 12:36.793
What th...?
I'm carter pewterschmidt!

12:36.861 --> 12:37.963
This is my company!

12:38.031 --> 12:39.267
Throw that guy out!

12:39.335 --> 12:40.437
Sorry,
mr. Pewterschmidt,

12:40.505 --> 12:42.176
But we work
for mr. Griffin now.

12:42.244 --> 12:43.714
You can't do
this to me!

12:43.782 --> 12:45.219
Do you know
who I am?!

12:45.286 --> 12:46.388
I'm carter
pewterschmidt!

12:46.457 --> 12:47.860
I'm not getting
in that elevator!

12:47.928 --> 12:50.033
Don't you dare throw
me out of this lobby!

12:50.101 --> 12:51.203
Don't you...
Damn it!

12:51.271 --> 12:52.909
Hey, what are you
doing out here?

12:52.977 --> 12:54.580
Joe:
I can't get in
the building!

12:54.648 --> 12:55.751
Uh, peggy?

12:55.819 --> 12:57.154
Peggy:
Yes, mr. Griffin.

12:57.223 --> 13:00.063
That fart I have at 3:00--
can you push that up to now?

13:00.132 --> 13:01.334
Very good, sir.

13:01.402 --> 13:03.374
(peter farts)

13:07.609 --> 13:09.781
Lois, how could you
let your idiot husband

13:09.849 --> 13:11.119
Take over my company?

13:11.186 --> 13:12.523
He fired all my staff,

13:12.591 --> 13:15.131
His stupid ideas are bankrupting
pewterschmidt industries,

13:15.198 --> 13:16.702
And now he won't step down!

13:16.771 --> 13:17.873
I know, daddy.

13:17.940 --> 13:19.544
He's become so full
of himself.

13:19.612 --> 13:22.286
He's more annoying than when
he's making his christmas list.

13:22.354 --> 13:25.429
Now, peter, are you sure this is
all you want for christmas?

13:25.496 --> 13:27.268
I'm only going
to the mall once.

13:27.336 --> 13:28.806
Yeah, yeah,
that's it.

13:28.873 --> 13:31.447
Man (on tv):
All new this christmas--
remote control cars...

13:31.515 --> 13:33.687
That glow in the dark?!

13:37.700 --> 13:39.638
Peter:
Get that!

13:39.706 --> 13:41.711
I've run that
company for 40 years.

13:41.780 --> 13:43.718
He even froze my
corporate bank accounts.

13:43.786 --> 13:44.955
I'm broke.

13:45.022 --> 13:46.125
Oh, that's ridiculous.

13:46.193 --> 13:48.499
I'll talk to him
as soon as he gets home.

13:48.566 --> 13:49.669
(jet plane approaching)

13:49.737 --> 13:50.906
What the hell is that?!

14:02.844 --> 14:03.979
Damn it, peter!

14:04.047 --> 14:06.152
Your plane set
my lawn on fire!

14:06.221 --> 14:07.691
Here, that ought
to cover it.

14:07.759 --> 14:09.463
Peter, I don't
want your money!

14:09.530 --> 14:12.070
Well, fine, then, have a box
of jeremy irons cereal.

14:12.139 --> 14:16.050
If you're looking for a prize
at the bottom, there is none.

14:16.117 --> 14:18.858
Only more cardboard.

14:18.925 --> 14:20.697
Peter, this has gone on
long enough.

14:20.764 --> 14:22.937
I want you to make things right
with daddy.

14:23.005 --> 14:24.107
It's his company.

14:24.175 --> 14:25.277
It's my company.

14:25.346 --> 14:26.448
It's your company.

14:26.516 --> 14:27.618
<i>Three's company.</i>

14:27.685 --> 14:29.925
Where the kisses are hers
and hers and his.

14:29.993 --> 14:31.329
What?
I'm sorry, lois.

14:31.397 --> 14:33.469
We all had some pot brownies
on the plane.

14:33.537 --> 14:35.174
Hey, peter,
are you seeing this rabbit?

14:35.242 --> 14:36.244
No.

14:36.312 --> 14:37.414
Well, I sure am.

14:37.482 --> 14:38.618
You know something?

14:38.686 --> 14:41.393
You're not qualified
to sit in that chair.

14:41.460 --> 14:43.667
Oh, aren't I?

14:43.734 --> 14:44.836
(screaming)

14:44.905 --> 14:46.074
(screaming)

14:46.142 --> 14:47.880
Maybe there's a rabbit
head under here.

14:47.948 --> 14:49.384
(yelling)

14:49.452 --> 14:53.229
Peter, all of my father's assets
are tied up in that corporation.

14:53.297 --> 14:54.767
If you freeze up his money,

14:54.835 --> 14:56.707
He's not gonna have anything
to live on.

14:56.774 --> 14:59.414
Now you are gonna make amends
with daddy, and that's final.

14:59.482 --> 15:01.454
All right, lois, if
that's what you want.

15:01.521 --> 15:04.162
Mr. Pewterschmidt, be
in my office tomorrow
morning at 9:00.

15:04.230 --> 15:06.837
I'm sure
we can figure something out.

15:06.904 --> 15:09.846
(evil laughter)

15:09.914 --> 15:12.554
Hmm... I don't know if I like
the sound of that laugh.

15:12.622 --> 15:14.862
I knew I didn't like
the sound of that laugh.

15:14.929 --> 15:16.065
Peter, this is
unacceptable.

15:16.133 --> 15:18.305
What gives you the right
to treat me like this?

15:18.373 --> 15:19.843
You've been treating me
like crap

15:19.911 --> 15:22.786
For 20 years, mr. Pewterschmidt,
and now I'm the one in charge.

15:22.853 --> 15:24.858
Hang on a second.

15:34.990 --> 15:36.327
Clean that up.

15:38.969 --> 15:40.239
Carter, as your boss,

15:40.307 --> 15:42.212
I command you
to have a viewing party

15:42.279 --> 15:44.284
<i>For tonight's episode
of the big bang theory,</i>

15:44.352 --> 15:46.825
And you have to go cubicle
to cubicle inviting people.

15:46.893 --> 15:49.601
Aw, come on, peter, I'm not,
I'm not good with rejection.

15:49.668 --> 15:51.540
I'm your boss.
Now do it!

15:54.015 --> 15:56.555
<i>Hi. I was gonna catch
the big bang theory tonight,</i>

15:56.623 --> 15:59.196
And wondered if you wanted
to come over and watch.

15:59.264 --> 16:00.734
Wha... What?
What is that?

16:00.803 --> 16:02.306
It's a comedy.
It's on cbs.

16:02.374 --> 16:03.476
I'm really into it.

16:03.544 --> 16:04.880
I don't want
to watch that.

16:04.948 --> 16:06.753
I don't want to
watch it with you.

16:06.821 --> 16:09.059
All right, if you change
your mind, here's a flyer.

16:09.128 --> 16:10.463
If you do decide to come,

16:10.531 --> 16:12.336
I'm just asking
that you bring an appetizer.

16:12.404 --> 16:13.740
Yeah, I'm not
gonna do that.

16:13.808 --> 16:16.048
See, peter, I told you,
no one wants to come.

16:16.115 --> 16:17.786
This is awful.
You're not
off the hook.

16:17.854 --> 16:19.324
You still got
to have that party.

16:19.391 --> 16:22.500
Babs, you want to
sit and watch...?

16:22.568 --> 16:23.938
No.

16:24.006 --> 16:26.379
I'll have you know
that I can bench press

16:26.447 --> 16:28.652
Over 690 billion nanograms.

16:28.721 --> 16:30.491
Sheldon, that's less
than two pounds.

16:30.559 --> 16:32.597
It sounded better
the way I said it.

16:32.666 --> 16:34.536
(laughs)

16:34.605 --> 16:37.345
Oh, when I tell that joke
at work tomorrow, people...

16:37.413 --> 16:39.486
People-people are gonna
be sorry they didn't come.

16:39.553 --> 16:41.024
They're-they're gonna...
This-this was...

16:41.091 --> 16:42.461
This-this was a good night.

16:45.070 --> 16:46.875
Carter, as your boss,
I'm ordering you

16:46.943 --> 16:50.151
To pay a compliment to this
sharply-dressed asian man.

16:50.218 --> 16:51.388
You look very nice.

16:51.456 --> 16:52.859
What else?

16:52.927 --> 16:54.197
Uh...
What about my shoe?

16:54.265 --> 16:55.367
They're nice, too.

16:55.435 --> 16:56.972
How you think
my house smell?

16:57.039 --> 16:58.209
Not oniony?

16:58.277 --> 16:59.647
You good man.

16:59.715 --> 17:02.856
I pat you on the head and
feed you from the hand.

17:07.772 --> 17:10.380
(crying):
And then he made me
clean out the fridge

17:10.447 --> 17:13.422
In the employee lounge, and
the employees were mad at me

17:13.490 --> 17:15.729
Because I-I threw out food
that they still wanted.

17:15.797 --> 17:17.200
I don't know
what's in there!

17:17.268 --> 17:18.370
Oh, that's it.

17:18.438 --> 17:19.941
Peter is completely
out of control.

17:20.009 --> 17:22.014
We've got to do something
to take him down

17:22.083 --> 17:23.519
And get your company back.

17:23.587 --> 17:24.890
Right, right. But how?

17:24.957 --> 17:26.394
In order to oust an idiot,

17:26.462 --> 17:28.167
We've got to think
like an idiot.

17:28.234 --> 17:29.438
Let's see.

17:29.505 --> 17:30.774
What's peter's weakness?

17:30.842 --> 17:32.847
He's got to have a weakness.

17:34.152 --> 17:35.489
Swamp monsters.

17:35.557 --> 17:38.331
Swamp monsters, of course!

17:40.873 --> 17:43.011
Lois, what are you doing here?

17:43.079 --> 17:45.653
Oh, I just wanted to make
sure everything was okay.

17:45.721 --> 17:47.693
Of course it's okay.
Why wouldn't it be?

17:47.760 --> 17:49.765
Oh, you know, that whole
swamp monster story.

17:49.833 --> 17:50.869
Swamp monster?

17:50.936 --> 17:52.708
You haven't heard?
Heard what?

17:52.775 --> 17:54.680
Oh, I'm sure
it's nothing.

17:54.748 --> 17:55.885
It's just, apparently,

17:55.952 --> 17:57.656
Somebody flushed a
baby swamp monster

17:57.724 --> 17:59.897
Down the toilet somewhere,
not far from here.

17:59.964 --> 18:02.772
What?! Who would flush
a baby swamp monster?

18:02.840 --> 18:04.377
Don't they know
what would happen?

18:04.444 --> 18:06.216
Well, apparently,
it has happened.

18:06.284 --> 18:07.486
And now it's grown up

18:07.554 --> 18:09.793
And is attacking
important businessmen.

18:09.861 --> 18:11.331
I'm an important
businessman!

18:11.399 --> 18:13.805
(deep growling)

18:13.873 --> 18:15.210
What the hell was that?!

18:15.277 --> 18:17.249
It sounds like maybe
a swamp monster

18:17.317 --> 18:19.222
Who needs to project
a little more.

18:19.289 --> 18:20.860
(deep growling)

18:20.928 --> 18:23.602
(roaring)

18:23.669 --> 18:24.772
Ah, crap!

18:24.840 --> 18:25.875
(roaring)

18:25.943 --> 18:27.513
Aah! A swamp monster!

18:27.581 --> 18:30.222
(swamp monster roars,
peter screams)

18:30.290 --> 18:31.727
Quick, peter, sign
this legal document

18:31.794 --> 18:34.602
Giving the company
back to daddy so you
won't get eaten!

18:34.670 --> 18:36.708
Oh, I don't understand,
but nothing makes sense

18:36.776 --> 18:38.346
In these swamp monster times.

18:38.414 --> 18:39.851
(screaming)

18:39.918 --> 18:41.423
We did it, daddy.

18:41.491 --> 18:44.197
I have my husband back,
and you have your company.

18:44.265 --> 18:45.903
Sorry I'm
late, lois.

18:45.971 --> 18:47.942
Okay, are we doing the
swamp monster thing?

18:48.010 --> 18:51.553
Wait, if you're daddy,
then who...?

18:51.621 --> 18:54.897
Both:
S-s-s-s-s-s-s...
Swamp monster!

18:58.175 --> 19:01.784
("scooby doo"-like
chase music playing)

19:20.442 --> 19:23.551
Now let's find out
who you really are.

19:23.619 --> 19:24.821
(gasps)
(gasps)

19:24.889 --> 19:25.992
Dr. House?!

19:26.059 --> 19:27.228
Indeed, lois.

19:27.296 --> 19:29.201
And if you don't mind,
I'll address you

19:29.269 --> 19:30.639
In my natural speaking voice,

19:30.706 --> 19:33.079
As I've grown so weary
of doing an american accent.

19:33.147 --> 19:34.249
Do you want to come

19:34.318 --> 19:36.122
<i>To my big bang
viewing party next week?</i>

19:36.190 --> 19:38.028
Daddy, you don't have
to do that anymore.

19:38.095 --> 19:40.202
I know, I know.
I-I... I like it now.

19:42.743 --> 19:44.715
Well, I'm sorry
you lost the company, peter,

19:44.783 --> 19:46.487
But I think it's for the best.

19:46.555 --> 19:48.494
You were turning
into a real jerk.

19:48.561 --> 19:49.763
Well, maybe so.

19:49.831 --> 19:52.572
But I sure am gonna miss
being a corporate big shot.

19:52.640 --> 19:55.581
Well, you'll always be a big
shot in this family, sweetheart.

19:55.649 --> 19:57.019
Thanks, honey.

19:57.087 --> 19:59.192
And I got a little
surprise for you.

19:59.261 --> 20:00.831
In that contract
you signed,

20:00.899 --> 20:02.770
You got to keep the
corporate plane.

20:02.838 --> 20:04.943
(gasps)
yeah!

20:08.521 --> 20:10.025
Peter, how are
you doing that?

20:10.093 --> 20:11.530
I-I don't...
I don't know, lois.

20:11.598 --> 20:12.533
I'm scared.

20:12.601 --> 20:13.670
Well, come down.

20:13.737 --> 20:15.207
I can't. I-I...
Get help.

20:15.275 --> 20:16.377
Call somebody.

20:16.446 --> 20:17.715
Wh-wh-who do I call?

20:17.783 --> 20:20.390
I-I don't know. A police...
A fireman... A scientist!

20:20.458 --> 20:21.627
Call a scientist!

20:21.695 --> 20:23.499
Okay, you kids stay here
with your father.

20:23.567 --> 20:25.873
I'm gonna go find
a scientist.

20:25.941 --> 20:27.946
Am I gonna die?

20:27.947 --> 21:28.947
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru